#!/usr/bin/env python3
# seat — run the CLI-only seats (Cursor, Devin) on registered accounts.
#
# Cursor and Devin traffic cannot pass through the LB: each CLI talks to its own
# backend on its own subscription. agent-lb still owns the accounts: this CLI keeps
# the registry, probes each account's auth, picks an account per dispatch, fails over
# on a limit or auth error, and writes receipts to the dispatch ledger. The LB reads
# the state file this CLI writes and serves it as the `cursor` and `devin` pools of
# /api/pools and as /api/pools/seat-accounts. Stdlib only, same family as `route`.
#
# Commands:
#   seat accounts [--json]                       registry, auth, cooldowns, observed usage
#   seat add <id> --vendor cursor|devin [--api-key-file F | --api-key-prompt] [--data-dir D]
#   seat probe [--vendor V] [--json]             auth status per account, written to state
#   seat lease --vendor V --for ID --ttl S --out DIR [--json]
#   seat release LEASE [--log FILE] [--outcome OUTCOME] [--json]
#   seat run --vendor V --model M [--account A] [--class C [--author-vendor V]] [--cwd D] [--mode ask|write]
#            [--timeout S] (--prompt-file F | -- <prompt>)
#            With --class (and no --account) the run first holds a `route reserve` lease, renews it while the
#            vendor CLI runs and releases it on exit; no capacity exits 4 and launches nothing (A4d). A signal
#            or a lost lease stops the CLI's process group; the release then runs to the end.
#
# Account auth (never printed, never written anywhere but the key file):
#   cursor  auth=login    the CLI's own login (`cursor-agent login`, macOS keychain). One per Mac:
#                         a second login replaces the first, so extra accounts use api-key.
#           auth=api-key  a Cursor user API key read from a 0600 key file into CURSOR_API_KEY,
#                         with its own CURSOR_CONFIG_DIR and AGENT_CLI_CREDENTIAL_STORE=memory.
#                         Without the memory store the CLI saves the key's tokens to the keychain
#                         and replaces the login account (cursor-agent 2026.09.23).
#   devin   auth=data-dir credentials.toml under XDG_DATA_HOME (default ~/.local/share).
#                         Log an extra account in with
#                         `XDG_DATA_HOME=<dir> devin auth login --force-manual-token-flow`.
#
# Env:
#   SEAT_HOME     registry, state and keys (default ~/.agent-lb/seats)
#   ROUTE_LEDGER  dispatch ledger (default ~/.claude/logs/dispatch.jsonl)
#   ROUTE_BIN     route CLI used to resolve family aliases (default ~/.agent-lb/bin/route)
#   SEAT_CURSOR_BIN / SEAT_DEVIN_BIN  CLI binaries (default cursor-agent / devin on PATH)
#
# 2026-10-01: a box's run also uses unexpired lease bundles under <seat_home>/leases/.
